The published mxlib documentation is located at: https://jaredmales.github.io/mxlib-doc/index.html

Steps to update (assuming you have access to the mxlib-doc repo):
1) clone the mxlib-doc repo (doesn't matter where)
2) delete all files in the mxlib-doc folder
3) in this directory, type make (requires doxygen)
4) copy contents of ./html to that repo (but not in a directory named html, rather at mxlib-doc/)
5) in mxlib-doc do `git add *`
6) in mxlib-doc do `git commit -a -m "updated docs"`
7) in mxlib-doc do `git push`
8) now you can delete your local mxlib-doc copy

To maintain the size of mxlib-doc at a manageable level:

```
git checkout --orphan temp <f>      # checkout to the status of the git repo at commit f; creating a branch named "temp"
git commit -m "new root commit"     # create a new commit that is to be the new root commit
git rebase --onto temp <f> master   # now rebase the part of history from <f> to master onthe temp branch
git branch -D temp                  # we don't need the temp branch anymore
git prune --progress                 # delete all the objects w/o references
git gc --aggressive                  # aggressively collect garbage; may take a lot of time on large repos

git push -f
```
